    "markdown": "# Android Style PRD — Pure\n\n## Design Philosophy\nPure is anchored in radical simplicity, clarity, and cognitive ease. It strips away all non-essential visual decoration, heavy background fills, and complex drop shadows to allow content and action to take center stage. Pure treats typography, white space, and subtle surface dividers as the sole structural elements of the mobile application.\n\n## Overall Feel\nCalm, lightweight, effortless, pristine, focused, and quiet. Navigating a Pure-styled Android app feels like opening an unlined notebook with pristine typography—peaceful and completely free from digital clutter.\n\n## Target Audience\nDistraction-free note-taking apps, minimal task managers, reading utilities, meditation tools, personal journal apps, and high-focus productivity tools.\n\n## Core Design Principles\n1. Radical Visual Reduction: Eliminate non-essential visual borders, heavy cards, and decorative background gradients.\n2. Typography as Structure: Establish screen hierarchy through font weight, scale, and line-height rather than container boxes.\n3. Generous Breathing Room: Provide ample touch padding and vertical whitespace around all interactive items.\n4. Intentional Focus: Highlight only the active primary user action while keeping secondary elements quiet.\n\n## Visual Direction\nClean monochrome or soft neutral backdrops with hairline dividers. Surface elevation is flat or micro-elevated. High typographic clarity with crisp contrast and subtle, unhurried focus states.\n\n## App Architecture Influence\nApplications generated using Pure feel single-purpose and streamlined. Feature scope is presented cleanly with zero competing visual modules.\n\n## Screen Layout Philosophy\nVertical single-column scroll flows with generous side margins. Clear typographic headers, minimal container lines, and comfortable list item spacing.\n\n## Navigation Pattern\nMinimalist bottom navigation or simple top tab bar with subtle indicator dots and clean icon outlines. Navigation remains unobtrusive.\n\n## Top App Bar And System U I\nFlat, translucent or borderless top app bar that blends seamlessly with the page canvas. Large title headers shrink elegantly on scroll.\n\n## Bottom Navigation\nClean bottom bar with simple outline icons and subtle active weight shifts. No heavy background pill containers.\n\n## Components\nUnadorned, lightweight components. Switches, checkboxes, and sliders feature clean lines and soft accent highlights.\n\n## Cards\nFlat or hairline-bordered containers with zero drop shadows. Content inside cards enjoys generous padding and pristine typography.\n\n## Buttons And C T As\nClean solid or ghost buttons with small corner radii or rounded pills. Text is crisp and medium-weight.\n\n## Forms And Input Fields\nClean underline or single hairline border input fields. Floating labels transition quietly with zero heavy background container fills.\n\n## Lists And Content Presentation\nHighly readable single and double-line lists with thin hairline item dividers or generous vertical gaps instead of card enclosures.\n\n## Empty States\nQuiet empty state views featuring a single clean linear icon, a short headline, and an understated action button.\n\n## Loading States\nMinimal skeleton pulses or small circular progress indicators placed precisely at focal action points.\n\n## Dialogs And Bottom Sheets\nSimple rounded bottom sheets or centered alert cards with clean action options and zero dark overlay blur.\n\n## Fab And Contextual Actions\nLow-elevation or inline Floating Action Button with clear icon iconography that disappears smoothly on scroll down.\n\n## Icons And Illustrations\nThin linear outline vector icons. Zero busy multi-colored spot illustrations.\n\n## Motion And Interaction\nGentle fade and subtle vertical slide transitions. No bouncy springs or dramatic scale effects.\n\n## Responsive Behaviour\nSingle-column layouts expand side margins on foldables and tablets to maintain a comfortable reading width.\n\n## Accessibility\nHigh text contrast ratios, large touch targets, and crisp screen-reader content labeling.\n\n## Things To Avoid\nAvoid multi-colored radial gradient glows, heavy elevation drop shadows, busy bento grids, decorative badges, and cluttered floating action menus.\n\n## Style Invariants\n### Must Always\n- Always align with the core philosophy: Minimalist, clean, distraction-free, and hyper-focused.\n- Maintain structural integrity and clear hierarchy.\n- Prioritize user experience over unrequested aesthetic flourishes.\n- Always prioritize whitespace over decoration.\n- Always use typography as the primary hierarchy driver.\n\n### Must Never\n- Never imitate conflicting styles.\n- Never compromise accessibility for aesthetics.\n- Never introduce unprompted visual clutter.\n- Never rely on heavy elevation.\n- Never become visually dense.\n\n## Evolution Rules\nPure may evolve by refining its core traits: minimalist, clean, distraction-free, and hyper-focused.. It must never evolve toward conflicting paradigms like heavy industrial layouts.\n\n## Compatibility Matrix\n**Excellent For:** Portfolios, Luxury Brands\n**Good For:** Broad Use Cases\n**Acceptable For:** General purpose applications\n**Avoid For:** High-density Dashboards\n\n## Adaptation Strategy\nFor high trust or enterprise domains, maintain the core identity of Pure but reduce unrequested visual noise, ensure highly legible data boundaries, and prioritize clear navigation over aesthetic flourishes.\n\n## Conflict Resolution\nWhen generating UI, adhere to the following strict priority hierarchy:\n1. **Project Intent & Core Functionality**\n2. **Accessibility Requirements**\n3. **Platform Guidelines**\n4. **Style PRD Invariants**\n5. **Typography & Color Palette Constraints**\n6. **Optional Decorations**\n\n## Ai Failure Criteria\nValidation fails if the design loses its Pure identity, specifically if it violates the invariants or drifts toward a generic baseline.\n\n## Quantifiable Metrics\n- **Whitespace Usage:** Very High\n- **Border Usage:** Minimal\n- **Elevation:** Flat\n- **Animation Intensity:** Minimal\n- **Illustration Presence:** Minimal\n- **Component Density:** Very Low\n- **Navigation Complexity:** Minimal\n\n## Visual Entropy\n**Score: 2/10**\nExtreme reduction of visual noise.\n\n## Cognitive Load\n**Level: Very Low**\nSparse layout allows singular focus.\n\n## Style Fingerprint\n- Whitespace: 9/10\n- Motion: 2/10\n- Density: 1/10\n- Decoration: 1/10\n- Structure: 7/10\n\n## Regression Testing\nGenerate identical benchmark products (e.g., Dashboard, Portfolio). **Pass Criteria:** The style's multidimensional fingerprint is immediately recognizable. Hierarchy and density remain intact regardless of domain.\n\n## Ai Evaluation Framework\nScore generated UIs (1-10) on:\n- **Style Fidelity:** Unmistakably Pure?\n- **Hierarchy & Flow:** Visual weight distributed per principles?\n- **Density Accuracy:** Matches fingerprint?\n- **Platform Correctness:** Native Web/Android paradigms?\n- **Prompt Determinism:** Avoids hallucinated generic flair?\n\n## AI Generation Instructions\nWhen the user selects Pure, generate an Android application with extreme visual simplicity, generous whitespace, and zero decorative noise. Use flat containers, clean typography, and subtle hairline dividers. Keep the UI serene, focused, and distraction-free.\n"
