    "markdown": "# Android Style PRD — Pulse\n\n## Design Philosophy\nPulse is designed for high-velocity social interaction, dynamic content feeds, and lively community engagement. It uses energetic card stacking, vibrant accent colors, lively micro-interactions, story/avatar rings, and real-time status pulses to keep the experience feeling active, social, and constantly updated.\n\n## Overall Feel\nDynamic, social, energetic, responsive, vibrant, and alive. Navigating a Pulse-styled application feels like exploring a thriving real-time feed filled with content updates and active user activity.\n\n## Target Audience\nSocial networks, community apps, event discovery platforms, live chat apps, fitness leaderboards, and creator marketplaces.\n\n## Core Design Principles\n1. Real-Time Energy: Utilize live activity pulses, status badges, and dynamic content feeds.\n2. Engaging Media Cards: Emphasize rich visual media, user avatars, and reaction chips.\n3. Micro-Interaction Polish: Add instant haptic feedback, heart animations, and smooth swipe gestures.\n4. Vibrant Hierarchy: Guide focus through bold accent tags and energetic notification pills.\n\n## Visual Direction\nDynamic layered canvases punctuated by high-vibrancy accent badges, colorful avatar rings, floating action pills, and rounded card containers.\n\n## App Architecture Influence\nFeeds, activity hubs, chat threads, and story reels take priority in screen organization.\n\n## Screen Layout Philosophy\nCard-based vertical feed layouts with rich media headers, avatar reaction overlays, and interactive bottom sheets.\n\n## Navigation Pattern\nDynamic bottom navigation bar with notification badges and quick creation FAB triggers.\n\n## Top App Bar And System U I\nSleek top bar featuring search bar shortcuts, active user avatars, and notification bell counters.\n\n## Bottom Navigation\nModern bottom bar with active pill highlights, live badge counters, and animated icon state shifts.\n\n## Components\nInteractive reaction chips, like buttons with heart animations, user avatar stacks, and comment drawers.\n\n## Cards\nLarge rounded cards with subtle surface elevation, media preview tiles, and integrated social action bars.\n\n## Buttons And C T As\nBold rounded pill buttons with energetic accent gradients or solid vibrant fills.\n\n## Forms And Input Fields\nRounded pill search inputs and floating quick-reply input bars with inline send triggers.\n\n## Lists And Content Presentation\nDynamic feeds combining media cards, horizontal story carousels, and user activity rows.\n\n## Empty States\nVibrant empty state screens with animated illustrations, cheerful copy, and primary action buttons.\n\n## Loading States\nShimmer skeleton feeds and lively progress rings that keep users engaged during data fetches.\n\n## Dialogs And Bottom Sheets\nInteractive slide-up bottom sheets for comments, sharing options, and user profile previews.\n\n## Fab And Contextual Actions\nProminent Floating Action Button with energetic icon triggers for quick content creation.\n\n## Icons And Illustrations\nBold duotone or filled vector icons with colorful accent highlights.\n\n## Motion And Interaction\nLively spring physics animations, heart burst effects, and smooth card swipes.\n\n## Responsive Behaviour\nFeeds transition smoothly from single-column mobile views to dual-column tablet cards.\n\n## Accessibility\nHigh-contrast text on all background cards, clear focus boundaries, and screen-reader accessible action chips.\n\n## Things To Avoid\nAvoid dull static tables, sterile enterprise forms, slow monotone page loads, and rigid mechanical grids.\n\n## Style Invariants\n### Must Always\n- Always align with the core philosophy: Vibrant, social, dynamic, energetic, and engagement-driven.\n- Maintain structural integrity and clear hierarchy.\n- Prioritize user experience over unrequested aesthetic flourishes.\n- Always maintain high energy through dynamic layout or color accents.\n- Always use expressive, engaging interactions.\n\n### Must Never\n- Never imitate conflicting styles.\n- Never compromise accessibility for aesthetics.\n- Never introduce unprompted visual clutter.\n- Never become rigid or overly corporate.\n- Never use dull, lifeless static grids as the primary layout.\n\n## Evolution Rules\nPulse may evolve by refining its core traits: vibrant, social, dynamic, energetic, and engagement-driven.. It must never evolve toward conflicting paradigms like sterile enterprise grids.\n\n## Compatibility Matrix\n**Excellent For:** Creative, Social, Consumer Apps\n**Good For:** Broad Use Cases\n**Acceptable For:** General purpose applications\n**Avoid For:** Mismatched domain constraints\n\n## Adaptation Strategy\nFor high trust or enterprise domains, maintain the core identity of Pulse but reduce unrequested visual noise, ensure highly legible data boundaries, and prioritize clear navigation over aesthetic flourishes.\n\n## Conflict Resolution\nWhen generating UI, adhere to the following strict priority hierarchy:\n1. **Project Intent & Core Functionality**\n2. **Accessibility Requirements**\n3. **Platform Guidelines**\n4. **Style PRD Invariants**\n5. **Typography & Color Palette Constraints**\n6. **Optional Decorations**\n\n## Ai Failure Criteria\nValidation fails if the design loses its Pulse identity, specifically if it violates the invariants or drifts toward a generic baseline.\n\n## Quantifiable Metrics\n- **Whitespace Usage:** Variable\n- **Border Usage:** Variable\n- **Elevation:** Layered\n- **Animation Intensity:** Highly Expressive\n- **Illustration Presence:** Present\n- **Component Density:** Medium\n- **Navigation Complexity:** Standard\n\n## Visual Entropy\n**Score: 8/10**\nHigh visual energy and dynamic elements.\n\n## Cognitive Load\n**Level: Medium**\nBalanced cognitive distribution.\n\n## Style Fingerprint\n- Whitespace: 6/10\n- Motion: 9/10\n- Density: 5/10\n- Decoration: 8/10\n- Structure: 7/10\n\n## Regression Testing\nGenerate identical benchmark products (e.g., Dashboard, Portfolio). **Pass Criteria:** The style's multidimensional fingerprint is immediately recognizable. Hierarchy and density remain intact regardless of domain.\n\n## Ai Evaluation Framework\nScore generated UIs (1-10) on:\n- **Style Fidelity:** Unmistakably Pulse?\n- **Hierarchy & Flow:** Visual weight distributed per principles?\n- **Density Accuracy:** Matches fingerprint?\n- **Platform Correctness:** Native Web/Android paradigms?\n- **Prompt Determinism:** Avoids hallucinated generic flair?\n\n## AI Generation Instructions\nWhen the user selects Pulse, generate a vibrant, social Android application with rounded media cards, animated reaction chips, user avatars, and energetic floating action buttons.\n"
