    "markdown": "# Android Style PRD — Flow\n\n## Design Philosophy\nFlow on Android is built on continuous native motion and organic fluidity. It replaces rigid segmented screens with a seamless journey where elements morph and expand gracefully. The interface feels like a single living surface rather than distinct disjointed pages.\n\n## Overall Feel\nFluid, seamless, continuous, organic, effortless, and connected. The app feels highly responsive, naturally guiding the user through tasks with intuitive gestures and unbroken momentum.\n\n## Target Audience\nConsumer lifestyle apps, immersive media players, wellness trackers, travel guides, and premium e-commerce experiences.\n\n## Core Design Principles\n1. Seamless Continuity: Use shared element transitions and expanding cards to navigate without breaking context.\n2. Organic Momentum: Use soft curves, overlapping layers, and natural scrolling rhythm.\n3. Fluid Gestures: Embrace native swipe and drag interactions that feel physically connected to the user's touch.\n4. Rhythmic Breathing: Balance content with expansive whitespace to prevent visual fatigue.\n\n## Visual Direction\nSoft, flowing surfaces adapting to the selected color palette. Gentle gradients, rounded corners, and soft elevation create a continuous, overlapping landscape.\n\n## App Architecture Influence\nNavigation relies less on abrupt jumps and more on expanding bottom sheets, modal morphs, and horizontal paging.\n\n## Screen Layout Philosophy\nFluid scrolling lists with overlapping headers. Elements bleed into the edges naturally.\n\n## Navigation Pattern\nFloating bottom navigation or gesture-based progression. Transitions between states are always animated.\n\n## Top App Bar And System U I\nSeamless, translucent app bars that blend into the scrollable content or collapse dynamically.\n\n## Bottom Navigation\nFloating or pill-shaped bottom bar that disappears smoothly on downward scroll to maximize content area.\n\n## Components\nRounded, organic UI components. Progress indicators are fluid bars or smooth rings.\n\n## Cards\nSoftly rounded cards that expand seamlessly into detail views when tapped.\n\n## Buttons And C T As\nFully rounded pill buttons with generous radii and liquid-like ripple feedback.\n\n## Forms And Input Fields\nSeamless input fields with soft focus rings and fluid inline validations.\n\n## Lists And Content Presentation\nFlowing lists where items glide into place. Dividers are avoided in favor of ample spacing.\n\n## Empty States\nOrganic, floating illustrations with a continuous, gentle pulse animation.\n\n## Loading States\nFluid shimmer effects and smooth liquid loaders.\n\n## Dialogs And Bottom Sheets\nBottom sheets slide up naturally with gesture tracking. Modals morph from the triggering element.\n\n## Fab And Contextual Actions\nFloating Action Button morphs into the creation screen using a seamless material transformation.\n\n## Icons And Illustrations\nSoft, rounded vector icons with unbroken strokes.\n\n## Motion And Interaction\nSmooth physics-based animations, liquid easing curves, and organic shared element transitions.\n\n## Responsive Behaviour\nFluid layouts adapt gracefully to foldables and tablets, utilizing overlapping panels instead of rigid columns.\n\n## Accessibility\nHigh-contrast text and clear focus boundaries maintained across fluid surfaces.\n\n## Things To Avoid\nAvoid rigid grid lines, abrupt screen cuts, sharp geometric corners, and disconnected modal pops.\n\n## Style Invariants\n### Must Always\n- Always align with the core philosophy: Fluid, continuous, seamless, organic, and effortlessly connected.\n- Maintain structural integrity and clear hierarchy.\n- Prioritize user experience over unrequested aesthetic flourishes.\n- Always use fluid, natural spacing and transitions.\n- Always prioritize a calm, continuous user journey.\n\n### Must Never\n- Never imitate conflicting styles.\n- Never compromise accessibility for aesthetics.\n- Never introduce unprompted visual clutter.\n- Never use harsh, rigid containers or sharp cutoffs.\n- Never rush animations or interactions.\n\n## Evolution Rules\nFlow may evolve by refining its core traits: fluid, continuous, seamless, organic, and effortlessly connected.. It must never evolve toward conflicting paradigms like generic minimal templates.\n\n## Compatibility Matrix\n**Excellent For:** Health, Wellness, Education\n**Good For:** Broad Use Cases\n**Acceptable For:** General purpose applications\n**Avoid For:** Mismatched domain constraints\n\n## Adaptation Strategy\nFor high trust or enterprise domains, maintain the core identity of Flow but reduce unrequested visual noise, ensure highly legible data boundaries, and prioritize clear navigation over aesthetic flourishes.\n\n## Conflict Resolution\nWhen generating UI, adhere to the following strict priority hierarchy:\n1. **Project Intent & Core Functionality**\n2. **Accessibility Requirements**\n3. **Platform Guidelines**\n4. **Style PRD Invariants**\n5. **Typography & Color Palette Constraints**\n6. **Optional Decorations**\n\n## Ai Failure Criteria\nValidation fails if the design loses its Flow identity, specifically if it violates the invariants or drifts toward a generic baseline.\n\n## Quantifiable Metrics\n- **Whitespace Usage:** Variable\n- **Border Usage:** Variable\n- **Elevation:** Variable\n- **Animation Intensity:** Moderate\n- **Illustration Presence:** Minimal\n- **Component Density:** Medium\n- **Navigation Complexity:** Standard\n\n## Visual Entropy\n**Score: 4/10**\nBalanced and structured.\n\n## Cognitive Load\n**Level: Medium**\nBalanced cognitive distribution.\n\n## Style Fingerprint\n- Whitespace: 6/10\n- Motion: 5/10\n- Density: 5/10\n- Decoration: 4/10\n- Structure: 4/10\n\n## Regression Testing\nGenerate identical benchmark products (e.g., Dashboard, Portfolio). **Pass Criteria:** The style's multidimensional fingerprint is immediately recognizable. Hierarchy and density remain intact regardless of domain.\n\n## Ai Evaluation Framework\nScore generated UIs (1-10) on:\n- **Style Fidelity:** Unmistakably Flow?\n- **Hierarchy & Flow:** Visual weight distributed per principles?\n- **Density Accuracy:** Matches fingerprint?\n- **Platform Correctness:** Native Web/Android paradigms?\n- **Prompt Determinism:** Avoids hallucinated generic flair?\n\n## AI Generation Instructions\nWhen generating an Android app in the Flow style, prioritize seamless continuity and organic momentum. Use shared element transitions, soft rounded containers, and overlapping layers. Implement fluid, physics-based motion and ensure the layout feels like a single continuous surface.\n"
